  DiamondBackgroundColor #FEF3C7
  DiamondBorderColor #B45309
  StartColor #15803D
  EndColor #B91C1C
  BarColor #64748B
}

title RecruitBook Batch 6 — Saved Shortlist Entry Renderability Decision

' ============================================================
' NOT a state machine — no named ShortlistEntry states, no
' lifecycle transitions, no state-model number. This is a
' single per-entry decision, re-evaluated fresh at query time
' for EVERY saved entry on EVERY read of the saved list.
' ============================================================

start
:Officer opens /admissions/dashboard\n"Saved students" section\n(one stored ShortlistEntry row under evaluation);

if (1. Access precondition:\nis_verified_admissions_officer()?) then (no)
  #FEE2E2:No saved-list access at all\n(not specific to any one entry);
  stop
else (yes)
endif

if (2. RLS SELECT ownership gate:\nadmissions_officer_application_user_id\n= current_application_user_id()?) then (no)
  #FEE2E2:Entry invisible to this caller\n(belongs to a different officer);
  stop
else (yes)
endif

if (3. Live visibility gate:\nis_admissions_visible_profile(\nstudent_profile_id)?) then (no)
  #FEE2E2:Entry silently ABSENT from the\nrendered list — no distinct stale\nstate, no reason shown, no count,\nno placeholder;
  stop
else (yes)
  #DCFCE7:Entry RENDERS — ONLY the four\napproved summary fields\n(preferredName, country,\ncityRegion, intendedMajor);
  stop
endif

note right
  This decision governs RENDERABILITY of an
  already-saved row in THIS ONE query only.
  The underlying ShortlistEntry row is never
  changed or deleted by this decision — only
  its visibility in the rendered list this time.
end note

note right
  Silent absence is indistinguishable across
  causes: "doesn't exist," "belongs to someone
  else," "hidden," "withdrawn," or "suspended
  owner" all look identical — no oracle.
end note

legend right
  Cross-cutting rules:
  * Gate 3 reuses the existing, unchanged Batch 5
    is_admissions_visible_profile(profile_id) helper —
    no new helper, no new state-model number.
  * Re-evaluated fresh on every read; no cached or
    derived visibility field exists anywhere.
  * No named/multiple Shortlist model, no Remove flow,
    and no student/counselor actor — see Group 1c/1e.
  --
  Resurfacing: because the row is never touched by
  this decision, a retained entry automatically
  resurfaces on a LATER query once the profile becomes
  effectively visible again — no re-save, no explicit
  "restore" action, no stored state transition.
  --
  Scope boundary: this decision governs the saved-LIST
  entry rendering only. The existing
  /admissions/students/[id] detail route independently
  re-gates with the SAME Batch 5 helper
  (is_admissions_visible_profile) on its own separate
  request — it does NOT share or trust this list-time
  decision's result.
endlegend

@enduml
